## Structure

- Root `build.gradle.kts`: plugins with `apply false` only — no dependencies
- Module scripts: Android plugin, namespace, SDK config, dependencies
- `settings.gradle.kts`: `FAIL_ON_PROJECT_REPOS`, filtered repositories

## Version catalog (mandatory)

- All versions in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`
- Reference as `libs.library.name` and `libs.plugins.name`
- **Never** hardcode `"group:artifact:version"` in module scripts

```kotlin
// ✅ GOOD
implementation(libs.androidx.core.ktx)

// ❌ BAD
implementation("androidx.core:core-ktx:1.12.0")
```

## SDK defaults (adjust only on project-wide request)

- minSdk = 24
- targetSdk / compileSdk = latest stable project uses
- Java 17 compatibility (`compileOptions`)
- Kotlin official code style

## Dependency scope

| Scope | When |
|-------|------|
| `implementation` | Default for almost everything |
| `api` | Rare — only when types must leak to consumers |
| `testImplementation` | Unit tests |
| `androidTestImplementation` | Instrumentation tests |

## Module rules

- Keep modules independent — no circular deps
- Feature modules must not depend on each other directly
- Enable View Binding on UI modules
- App release: minify + shrink; library modules: minify off

## Build types

- Debug: no minify, optional `applicationIdSuffix`
- Release: minify + ProGuard/R8 on app module
- Secrets and signing credentials in `local.properties` or CI env — not in source

## ProGuard

- Keep rules in app module only unless module-specific needs arise
- Preserve domain entities and MVI state/intent/effect classes
